{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>They turn back, etc.</b> The meaning: I — I have power when I will it, not the idols." "<b>[The molten image].</b> It draws after it its nation, and likewise [it is] 'the molten image of the mask,' on account of the word אתם."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {1 "The Hebrew phrase לפסילי המסכה is translated hyper-literally; its meaning is obscure and possibly textually problematic."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:35.448933423Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}